Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Salt in the Skillet, Water at the Gate
- Story & Context: On the night the power grid succumbed to the rising lake, Deacon Silas refused to abandon his cast-iron frying pan or his sound rig as the top floor of the Spire began to flood. While rain lashed through the broken floor-to-ceiling windows, Naledi slammed a dry 112 BPM log-drum pattern against the sound of sizzling lard and rising tide, creating the very first Silt-Stitch record on a battery-powered tape deck. The track captures the exact moment the water breached the threshold, marked by a screaming, distorted Theremin bend that mimicked the dying siren of the city's emergency broadcast. "Keep the grease hot child, the lake don't care how we fry," Silas rasped into a crackling Shure Green Bullet microphone as the floor beneath them vibrated with sub-bass.
